  partName: Valve Stem (2)
  description: The Valve Stem (2) is a tiny, elongated component situated at the
    top-center-front of the engine, constructed from Frame material, which acts as
    the link between the valve and the camshaft. Its role is critical, as it enables
    the valve to open and close in synchronization with the engine's firing sequence,
    and an interesting detail is that it is designed to rotate at high speeds, typically
    up to 5,000 rpm. The valve stem's location at the top-center-front allows for
    efficient transmission of motion to the valve.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
